  "style": "Painterly historical 4X diorama with north-west light, readable biome materials and transparent miniature map objects",
  "naturalObjectsV8Notes": "Each terrain-oriented natural-object atlas has exactly sixteen isolated alpha sprites. They contain no terrain, ground plane, continuous baseline, or painted contact shadows; the Phaser renderer composes them deterministically into visible chunk RenderTextures. Mountain massifs and ridges use a dedicated mountain atlas, glacial mountain peaks use a dedicated ice-and-glacier atlas, while highland is reserved for smaller rock outcrops.",
  "terrainV7Notes": "Original terrain materials use one maximum-quality WebP bitmap frame per terrain type. No mirrored, quilted, shader-generated, or coordinate-field variants are produced; no reference pixels are shipped.",
  "terrainChoiceHexesV1Notes": "Eight project-owned 4x4 terrain-material selection sheets are deterministically sliced into sixteen 112x128 pointy-top hex PNG frames per terrain family. The assets are a selection catalogue only: the runtime continues to load one explicitly chosen canonical terrain frame per type and does not randomize material variants.",
